A||||7||rodmcneill||Wheel cleaning||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||04-24-2001||03:24 AM||||Is there an easy way (or easier} to keep GT honeycomb wheels clean. Do any of the spray or foam cleaners work well? I have used toothbrushes (old ones) small brushes, small pieces of sponge but it takes forever. I tried one brand of wheel cleaner, I wasn't real impressed. This is one of the reasons I will eventually change to custom wheels.||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-24-2001||07:51 AM||||What brand did you try?  I use Wesley's Bleche-Wite (no, I can spell that's just the name of it) and have used it for a long time.  I have had very good luck with it, give it a try if it isnt the one you said you already did.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Fiero87311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto near completion!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierodave2001||04-24-2001||08:19 AM||||Ahh  a good question.  I've gone the tooth brush route also. (hope I used the old one !)<P>I've heard of two types of wheel cleaners on the market.  I was told to look out for the ones that could damage the paint/clear coat ?<P>Hope others can post more on this, 'cause it <BR>would save much time per wheel detailing out the car.<p>[This message has been edited by Fierodave2001 (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||rogergarrison||04-24-2001||09:57 AM||||I just use soap n water, or Eagle-One if there really dirty and a soft bristle brush. whatever you do, dont use any of those disks that go over rotor to keep wheels clean (aka Kleen Wheels, etc). Youll just toast your rotors.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroHarry||04-24-2001||10:16 AM||||Seem's that nothing short of highly acidic cleaners get "all" the brake dust off.<BR>I have been using that green 2001 stuff found in most local National chain part stores it seems to work well but still requires effort on my part.<BR>Just watch very closely for cleaners that have strong citrus acids, they can damage paint very easily if left on for any amount of time....................<P>------------------<BR>Harry<BR>FOCOSEVA<BR>1985 GT 258K+ "TEMPTATION"||||reg||8
Z||000005||Ronnie||04-24-2001||09:24 PM||||PuplePower works good to cut the dirt , but I wouldn't let it stay on the wheel for any amount of time, just enough to sprsy on , scrub with brush and hose off.||||reg||1
Z||000006||jaguiler||04-24-2001||10:40 PM||||cleaned my wheels this weekend with soap and water... my car looks new!<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||04-24-2001||11:00 PM||||I like to use those high pressure sprayers at the local car wash.  Might have to push the car up though to move the wheel, if you don't you will have one side very clean and the other side still dirty.<P>||||reg||1
